+     ```scala

=     and a negative numerator or denominator moves the sign: `-5 \ 3` is `Q64(-5, 3)`.
=
=     ```scala
-     import soundness.*
+     import soundness.*

-     1 \ 3 + 1 \ 6          // Q64(1, 2)
+     1 \ 3 + 1 \ 6          // Q64(1, 2)

-     (1 \ 0).nar            // true
+     (1 \ 0).nar            // true

-     3L \ 4L                // Q64(3, 4)
+     3L \ 4L                // Q64(3, 4)

=     3L \ 4L                // Q64(3, 4)
-     ```
+     ```

- entry .apply   `Short(bits)`, `Int(bits)`, `Long(bits)`, `Double(long)`, and the big-endian reads `Short(bytes)`, `Int(bytes)`, `Long(bytes)`
-     Extensions on the companions of the primitives. `Short(bits: B16)`, `Int(bits: B32)` and
-     `Long(bits: B64)` reinterpret a pattern as the primitive, free; `Double(long)` is
-     `Double.longBitsToDouble`; and `Short(bytes)`, `Int(bytes)` and `Long(bytes)` read the
-     first 2, 4 or 8 bytes of a frozen `Array[Byte]^{}` as a big-endian integer. They are
-     not exported to the `soundness` umbrella, so they need `import hypotenuse.*`.
+ entry .apply   `Short(bits)`, `Int(bits)`, `Long(bits)`, `Double(long)`, y las lecturas big-endian `Short(bytes)`, `Int(bytes)`, `Long(bytes)`
+     Extensiones sobre los objetos compañeros de los primitivos. `Short(bits: B16)`,
+     `Int(bits: B32)` y `Long(bits: B64)` reinterpretan un patrón como el primitivo, sin coste;
+     `Double(long)` es `Double.longBitsToDouble`; y `Short(bytes)`, `Int(bytes)` y
+     `Long(bytes)` leen los primeros 2, 4 u 8 bytes de un `Array[Byte]^{}` congelado como un
+     entero big-endian. No se exportan al paraguas `soundness`, así que necesitan
+     `import hypotenuse.*`.

- entry .erf   the Gauss error function, `erf(x)`, to about seven decimal places
-     The Abramowitz and Stegun rational approximation (formula 7.1.26), whose absolute error
-     is below `1.5 × 10⁻⁷` everywhere. `erf(0.0)` is `0.0` and `erf(x)` tends to `±1`.
+ entry .erf   la función de error de Gauss, `erf(x)`, con unas siete cifras decimales
+     La aproximación racional de Abramowitz y Stegun (fórmula 7.1.26), cuyo error absoluto
+     está por debajo de `1.5 × 10⁻⁷` en todas partes. `erf(0.0)` es `0.0` y `erf(x)` tiende a
+     `±1`.

