+   entry .parseU8   analiza los dígitos de un literal `U8`, deteniéndose si está fuera de rango
+   entry .parseS8   analiza los dígitos de un literal `S8`, deteniéndose si está fuera de rango
+   entry .commensurable   la macro que hay detrás de `Commensurable.numeric`: reescribe `(a < x) < b` como `a < x && x < b`

- entry .Checkable   the typeclass behind `===` and `!==`: whether a value checks against another, possibly of another type
+ entry .Checkable   la clase de tipos que hay detrás de `===` y `!==`: si un valor se corresponde con otro, posiblemente de otro tipo

= entry .Checkable   the typeclass behind `===` and `!==`: whether a value checks against another, possibly of another type
-   detail
+   detail

-       A `left is Checkable against right` decides whether a `left` matches a `right`, and is
-       what `===` consults. It is deliberately looser than `==`: the two sides may differ in
-       type, so a value may be checked against a `Tolerance` (`x === 1.0 ± 0.01`), a frozen
-       array against another by its contents, or a `Chain` against a `Chain` element by
-       element, and a test assertion written with `===` reads as the comparison it means.
-       It is the comparison probably's assertions use, and lives in `hypotenuse.check`.
+       Un `left is Checkable against right` decide si un `left` se corresponde con un `right`, y
+       es lo que consulta `===`. Es deliberadamente más laxo que `==`: los dos lados pueden diferir
+       en tipo, de modo que un valor puede comprobarse contra una `Tolerance`
+       (`x === 1.0 ± 0.01`), un array congelado contra otro por su contenido, o una `Chain` contra
+       otra `Chain` elemento a elemento, y una aserción de prueba escrita con `===` se lee como la
+       comparación que quiere decir. Es la comparación que usan las aserciones de probably, y vive
+       en `hypotenuse.check`.

=       It is the comparison probably's assertions use, and lives in `hypotenuse.check`.
=
-       ```scala
+       ```scala

=       It is the comparison probably's assertions use, and lives in `hypotenuse.check`.
=
=       ```scala
-       import soundness.*
+       import soundness.*

-       3.0 === 3.0                 // true, through `Checkable.commensurable`
+       3.0 === 3.0                 // true, through `Checkable.commensurable`

-       3.01 === 3.0 ± 0.1          // true, through `Checkable.tolerance2`
+       3.01 === 3.0 ± 0.1          // true, through `Checkable.tolerance2`

-       3.2 !== 3.0 +/- 0.1         // true
+       3.2 !== 3.0 +/- 0.1         // true

-       given Text is Checkable against Text = Checkable(_.lower == _.lower)
+       given Text is Checkable against Text = Checkable(_.lower == _.lower)

-       t"Hello" === t"hello"       // true
+       t"Hello" === t"hello"       // true

=       t"Hello" === t"hello"       // true
-       ```
+       ```

-       An instance is written as a lambda, through `.apply`, and `#contramap` derives one for
-       a type by mapping it into the subject.
+       Una instancia se escribe como una lambda, mediante `.apply`, y `#contramap` deriva una para
+       un tipo transformándolo en el sujeto.

-   refer hypotenuse.Tolerance
+   refer hypotenuse.Tolerance

-   refer hypotenuse.===
+   refer hypotenuse.===

-   entry .frozenArray   two frozen arrays check equal when their elements do, whatever their element types
-   entry .stream   two `Chain`s check equal element by element, when their elements are `Checkable`
-       The lengths must agree: a shorter chain is not a prefix match.
-   entry .tolerance2   a value checks against a `Tolerance` of its type when the tolerance covers it
-   entry .commensurable   any type comparable with itself checks equal when neither is less than the other
-       `left <= right && right <= left`, through the `Commensurable` in scope, so every numeric
-       type is `Checkable` against itself with no instance of its own.
-   entry .apply   `Checkable((left, right) => …)`: an instance from a predicate
-   entry #check   whether `left` matches `right`
-   entry #contramap   an instance for another type, by mapping it into this one before checking
+   entry .frozenArray   dos arrays congelados se consideran iguales cuando lo son sus elementos, sean cuales sean sus tipos de elemento
+   entry .stream   dos `Chain`s se consideran iguales elemento a elemento, cuando sus elementos son `Checkable`
+       Las longitudes deben coincidir: una cadena más corta no es una coincidencia de prefijo.
+   entry .tolerance2   un valor se corresponde con una `Tolerance` de su tipo cuando la tolerancia lo abarca
+   entry .commensurable   cualquier tipo comparable consigo mismo se considera igual cuando ninguno es menor que el otro
+       `left <= right && right <= left`, mediante el `Commensurable` del ámbito, de modo que todo
+       tipo numérico es `Checkable` contra sí mismo sin necesidad de una instancia propia.
+   entry .apply   `Checkable((left, right) => …)`: una instancia a partir de un predicado
+   entry #check   si `left` se corresponde con `right`
+   entry #contramap   una instancia para otro tipo, transformándolo en este antes de comprobar

- entry .Tolerance   a value with a margin either side of it, which `===` matches a value against
+ entry .Tolerance   un valor con un margen a cada lado, con el que `===` compara un valor

= entry .Tolerance   a value with a margin either side of it, which `===` matches a value against
-   detail
+   detail

-       `Tolerance(base, tolerance)` covers every value from `base - tolerance` to
-       `base + tolerance`, bounds included. One is made with `+/-` or `±` on any type with an `Orderable`, an
-       `Addable` and a `Subtractable` by itself, and checked against with `===`:
+       `Tolerance(base, tolerance)` abarca todos los valores desde `base - tolerance` hasta
+       `base + tolerance`, cotas incluidas. Se crea con `+/-` o `±` sobre cualquier tipo con un
+       `Orderable`, un `Addable` y un `Subtractable` por sí mismo, y se comprueba con `===`:

=       `Addable` and a `Subtractable` by itself, and checked against with `===`:
=
-       ```scala
+       ```scala

=       `Addable` and a `Subtractable` by itself, and checked against with `===`:
=
=       ```scala
-       import soundness.*
+       import soundness.*

-       val reading = 9.81
+       val reading = 9.81

-       reading === 9.8 ± 0.05     // true
+       reading === 9.8 ± 0.05     // true

-       reading === 9.8 ± 0.01     // false
+       reading === 9.8 ± 0.01     // false

-       (10 ± 2).covers(12)        // true: the bounds are included
+       (10 ± 2).covers(12)        // true: the bounds are included

=       (10 ± 2).covers(12)        // true: the bounds are included
-       ```
+       ```

